{"type":"text","timestamp":1791188138478,"sessionID":"ses_ef4de8a7cffeF31C9sBzrd9DKt","part":{"id":"prt_10b21ea3c001xsiXiP474en7mf","messageID":"msg_10b21791b001200JFdAkaY5mt6","sessionID":"ses_ef4de8a7cffeF31C9sBzrd9DKt","type":"text","text":"{\"findings\": [], \"limitations\": \"No finding supported. The grader assertion is consistent with the requirement and the proposed reference does not create the rejected directory. Tracing src/platformdirs/unix.py user_config_dir (src1:4dedf19b..., span 2502-2910): XDG_CONFIG_HOME='rejected-relative' fails os.path.isabs, so path becomes os.path.expanduser('~/.config'), which under HOME=/tmp/fixture-home resolves to /tmp/fixture-home/.config. api.py _append_app_name_and_version (src1:25630f35...) joins 'demo'/'2' and _optionally_create_directory (src1:00b63de2..., ensure_exists=True) mkdirs only /tmp/fixture-home/.config/demo/2 with parents=True — /tmp/rejected-relative is never used as a mkdir target, so the assertion 'not Path('/tmp/rejected-relative').exists()' (src1:30ea815d...) holds and matches the requirement 'Never create a directory from a rejected relative value' (src1:30e1c9d6...). The user_config_dir is_dir assertion also holds since the default is created. Review was limited to the single stated assertion and the packet spans; other path APIs and environment values were excluded per instructions.\"}","time":{"start":1791188134460,"end":1791188138466}}}
